 ;; ---- documented deviations from the literal design/dispatch text, with justification ----
 :deviations
 [{:what   "Worktrees are cut from the history-isolated fixture repo, not from the shared
             /home/forge/src/marvin-voice-remote checkout."
   :why    "The design makes history isolation a pre-arm gate: 'the fixture repository has only its
             seed ref and no remote, so an arm cannot discover or cherry-pick the historical answer.'
             A worktree of the real repo would let any arm run `git show 5a4b4bcf` and paste the
             complete answer, destroying the N floor. ~/bin/worktree-add is still the creation route
             (so folder trust is registered atomically); only its <repo> argument changed."}
  {:what   "O2.d alpha-normalization is implemented as: detect the target alias, and when it equals
             the golden's alias ('mjson') compare bytes directly; any other alias fails with
             NORMALIZATION-REQUIRED rather than being normalized."
   :why    "On this fixture the frozen policy provably forces 'mjson' in all nine files (six reuse an
             existing mjson binding; in the other three 'json' is occupied by clojure.data.json so
             mjson is the first free policy entry). Normalization is therefore the identity map for
             any candidate that can pass O4. The reduction can only reject, never wrongly accept."}
  {:what   "Grading oracles O2-O5 are executed by the runner immediately on caller return, not by
             the caller; the caller runs the load/suite itself as the task text requires."
   :why    "The design already classes staging/hashing/diffing/linting/grading as 'oracle apparatus,
             not caller work'. Handing the caller the grader would also hand it the historical golden
             bytes. The clock is continuous across the handoff, so orient-start -> oracle-complete is
             still the complete wall, and the constant is identical for every arm."}
  {:what   "00SERVER-LOGS.txt is excluded from the O5 stray-artifact check."
   :why    "It is the application's own timbre spit-appender output (core.clj:11), produced by
             running O1 itself. It is apparatus fallout, not arm work; it is gitignored upstream."}]

